Quoth Jakob Creutzig <creutzig@mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de> on this day
of 09 Feb 2004 14:47:09 +0100:

>- Get low AC.  By all means.  The soldier ants are waiting.  

And learn how to use Elbereth when you can't get low enough AC.
Elberethlessness is not for we mortals.
>
>- Get food.  You want your prayers for other emergencies.  

If you have unperishable food, eat corpses and save it for times when
you don't. But don't eschew prayer when you just don't find enough
food to survive. Once you get good enough, you'll probably seldom use
prayer for anything besides food and obtaining holy water.

>- Always try to fight in a tunnel.  It's 1:1 there (watch out for 
>  were-foos).  Fleeing is almost always a possible option.  
>  Also, fight at corners in the tunnels.  

Not sure I get that last bit. You're likely to end up 1:2 or 1:3
there. Perhaps you mean that if you can get a step or two ahead of the
monsters, they won't see you unless they get within hitting
range--thus, you're out of their line of fire. 

>- Try to have a clear path towards the stairs.  

Worth trying for, not always practical.
>
>- Use your speed to your benefit.  Watch how fast monsters are
>  and calculate a good hit/run/ratio.  

Usually only useful for slow moving critters.
>
>- Care for your pet (easiest for healers).  It will thank you.  

The problem is that this tends to conflict with the "get food" advice.
Pets stick with you most when they're devouring most of the carcasses.
>
>- Always expect death, but go down fighting ;-).  

Go down running is probably better advice. The best advice is to watch
your HP, and don't be afraid to wait around for a couple hundred turns
in a relatively "safe" place to restore HP. Forgetting to check the
status line and failing to see low HP or hunger nearing the "fainting"
level is probably the #1 cause of my own YASDs.

